WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:05.870
It’s not easy being in charge; you have
to make all the big decisions, like what’s

00:00:05.870 --> 00:00:09.840
best for everyone, how to improve things and
who gets the last bit of cake.

00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:14.639
In the modern world, we the people generally
get some kind of say in who makes those decisions.

00:00:14.639 --> 00:00:16.760
Well, most of the time at least.

00:00:16.760 --> 00:00:21.270
In the past however, you were generally stuck
with royal lineage or whatever leader had

00:00:21.270 --> 00:00:26.020
just murdered the previous boss and was now
using their head as a footstool.

00:00:26.020 --> 00:00:30.130
Sometimes, leaders took this responsibility
well and tried to be just and fair.

00:00:30.130 --> 00:00:35.390
But pretty often, they jumped head first into
the crazy pool and never bothered coming up

00:00:35.390 --> 00:00:36.390
for air.

00:00:36.390 --> 00:00:41.219
Today we look at some of the most psychopathic,
murderous and downright bananas rulers of

00:00:41.219 --> 00:00:47.230
the ancient world.

00:00:47.230 --> 00:00:52.520
If you’ve never heard of Ivan the Terrible,
his name is a pretty hefty clue that he wasn’t

00:00:52.520 --> 00:00:54.860
exactly the most agreeable of guys.

00:00:54.860 --> 00:01:01.440
Ivan IV was the Russian Tsar from 1547 to
1584, when he died from a stroke while playing

00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:04.799
chess; it’s a dangerous game kids, you’ve
been warned.

00:01:04.799 --> 00:01:09.909
Ivan was a leader of sorts from a very young
age, following his father as Grand Prince

00:01:09.909 --> 00:01:14.719
of Muscovy in 1533, a historical area around
Moscow.

00:01:14.719 --> 00:01:18.869
This was at the tender age of three when papa
died of a leg infection.

00:01:18.869 --> 00:01:23.649
His mother went soon after, when he was eight,
but this was a suspected poisoning.

00:01:23.649 --> 00:01:28.829
When Ivan was 16 he crowned himself Tsar of
all Russia, which at this point was a series

00:01:28.829 --> 00:01:31.430
of territories run by different rulers.

00:01:31.430 --> 00:01:36.759
Despite being a devout Christian, Ivan was
a little unstable, probably not helped by

00:01:36.759 --> 00:01:40.859
all the leg and poison related deaths of his
parents and his first wife.

00:01:40.859 --> 00:01:48.239
As a youngster he was said to have entertained
himself by tossing puppies off balconies.

00:01:48.239 --> 00:01:56.229
And as he expanded his kingdom, taking on
the Turks, the Kazan, the Crimean Tatars and

00:01:56.229 --> 00:01:59.719
many others, he enjoyed dealing out a good
punishment.

00:01:59.719 --> 00:02:05.159
He would wall up entire cities so his troops
could bring a good 500 to 1000 prisoners out

00:02:05.159 --> 00:02:11.739
every day and impale them or actually cook
them to death in giant frying pans.

00:02:11.739 --> 00:02:16.010
Since he was a family man, he’d bring his
son along to watch, but eventually he killed

00:02:16.010 --> 00:02:20.510
him too when he beat him round the head with
a pointed staff during a family feud.

00:02:20.510 --> 00:02:24.220
Makes your Christmas dinners arguments seems
a little better now, doesn’t it?

00:02:24.220 --> 00:02:30.200
Tamerlane the Great sounds a little friendlier
but he was one of the world’s biggest mass-murders.

00:02:30.200 --> 00:02:36.390
Mao Zedong may have overseen up to 75 million
deaths but Tamerlane’s 15 to 20 million

00:02:36.390 --> 00:02:42.830
is staggering considering there were only
some 350 million people on earth at that point.

00:02:42.830 --> 00:02:46.709
He wiped out 5% of the entire global population.

00:02:46.709 --> 00:02:50.900
And that’s without bombs or guns; you’ve
really got to applaud the hard-work and dedication

00:02:50.900 --> 00:02:52.569
he must have put in.

00:02:52.569 --> 00:02:58.319
Tamerlane, also known as Timur, founded the
Timurid Empire at the end of the 14th century

00:02:58.319 --> 00:03:03.530
and claimed to be descended from Ghengis Khan,
who came about 200 years before and was also

00:03:03.530 --> 00:03:05.480
pretty handy at the genocide game.

00:03:05.480 --> 00:03:07.859
We’ve all got to have heroes, right?

00:03:07.859 --> 00:03:12.379
Khan’s Mongol empire covered a much larger
area than Tamerlane’s and his armies are

00:03:12.379 --> 00:03:15.680
thought to have slaughtered almost 60 million.

00:03:15.680 --> 00:03:20.480
Tamerlane declared himself the “Sword of
Islam” and tried to rebuild the Mongol empire

00:03:20.480 --> 00:03:21.700
under his religion.

00:03:21.700 --> 00:03:28.280
But he wasn’t exactly at his most saintly
when he had 90,000 people in Baghdad beheaded

00:03:28.280 --> 00:03:31.959
or when he forced people to die of slow suffocation.

00:03:31.959 --> 00:03:37.079
He also had great towers built from his enemy’s
skulls, so he was pretty good at recycling

00:03:37.079 --> 00:03:38.219
too.

00:03:38.219 --> 00:03:43.139
Vlad the Impaler also has one of those delightfully
informative names.

00:03:43.139 --> 00:03:48.139
Vlad was part of the House of Drăculești
and ruled Transylvania in the 15th century.

00:03:48.139 --> 00:03:53.170
If this all sound a little familiar it’s
because he is the inspiration for Bram Stoker’s

00:03:53.170 --> 00:03:54.569
novel, Dracula.

00:03:54.569 --> 00:03:59.829
Vlad set about protecting his people and Christianity
from the surrounding Ottoman forces and did

00:03:59.829 --> 00:04:01.269
a pretty good job of it.

00:04:01.269 --> 00:04:06.819
He built a fearsome reputation, largely thanks
to his hobby of… you guessed it… impaling

00:04:06.819 --> 00:04:07.819
people.

00:04:07.819 --> 00:04:13.810
He once put all 20,000 men, women and children
of the city of Amlas on spiked sticks through

00:04:13.810 --> 00:04:14.989
their bodies and faces.

00:04:14.989 --> 00:04:18.729
But I don’t want you to think he was a one-trick
pony.

00:04:18.729 --> 00:04:23.560
He also skinned, boiled, decapitated, blinded,
strangled, hanged, burned, roasted, hacked,

00:04:23.560 --> 00:04:30.880
nailed, and buried alive, which sounds like
the menu at some kind of hipster pop-up restaurant;

00:04:30.880 --> 00:04:36.419
I’ll have the strangled rabbit with buried
aubergine please, with a side of forced rhubarb.

00:04:36.419 --> 00:04:41.990
And for desert, Vlad’s own head would fit
the bill as it’s said he was decapitated

00:04:41.990 --> 00:04:46.680
by the Turks and it was sent to Constantinople
in a jar of honey.

00:04:46.680 --> 00:04:50.930
The Roman Empire had a pretty good run of
crazy rulers so it’s hard to pick a worst

00:04:50.930 --> 00:04:56.941
one but today we’re going for Caligula thanks
to quotes such as “I wish Rome had but one

00:04:56.941 --> 00:05:00.669
neck, so that I could cut off all their heads
with one blow!”

00:05:00.669 --> 00:05:07.050
He was the 3rd Emperor of Rome from AD 37
to AD 41 and got the nickname Caligula, meaning

00:05:07.050 --> 00:05:12.340
Little Boots, from his time as a boy when
he accompanied his father, the general Germanicus,

00:05:12.340 --> 00:05:14.090
to various battles.

00:05:14.090 --> 00:05:19.060
He took over Rome from Tiberius and it’s
unclear whether he assassinated his predecessor

00:05:19.060 --> 00:05:21.930
or not but it wouldn’t be that unlikely.

00:05:21.930 --> 00:05:27.220
He then proceeded to spend just under 4 years
turning the palace into a giant brothel and

00:05:27.220 --> 00:05:33.020
having anyone around him put to death if he
was angry or bored or just had a few minutes

00:05:33.020 --> 00:05:34.020
to spare.

00:05:34.020 --> 00:05:39.530
He was eventually assassinated by conspirators
who wanted to restore the Roman republic but

00:05:39.530 --> 00:05:42.099
this failed and another emperor was installed
instead.

00:05:42.099 --> 00:05:46.640
If you’re going to come up with a secret
plan to overturn the Roman government then

00:05:46.640 --> 00:05:51.789
have a follow up plan at least, what would
the People’s Front of Judea think…

00:05:51.789 --> 00:05:57.600
Aside from his notorious cruelty and obsession
with rather suspicious hanky panky, he also

00:05:57.600 --> 00:06:03.930
appointed his favourite horse, Incitatus,
as an official priest, not the most stable

00:06:03.930 --> 00:06:05.820
decision.

00:06:05.820 --> 00:06:10.520
Not to be out done by all the men, we have
a female tyrant on the list as well.

00:06:10.520 --> 00:06:17.970
Empress Wu ruled China from 690 to 705 and
is the only woman in Chinese history to have

00:06:17.970 --> 00:06:19.590
power in her own right.

00:06:19.590 --> 00:06:24.990
And she made sure she wouldn’t be forgotten
as she was a ruthless and psychotic leader

00:06:24.990 --> 00:06:27.509
who drove her own people into misery.

00:06:27.509 --> 00:06:32.760
She was renowned for ordering daily tortures
and forced suicides, as well as her sexual

00:06:32.760 --> 00:06:34.090
depravity.

00:06:34.090 --> 00:06:39.740
Wu started life in court as a concubine for
Emperor Taizong and somehow managed to escape

00:06:39.740 --> 00:06:44.349
her expected retirement of going to the nunnery
after the Emperor died.

00:06:44.349 --> 00:06:49.819
Instead, even though it was frowned upon,
she became a concubine for his son, Emperor

00:06:49.819 --> 00:06:50.819
Gaozong.

00:06:50.819 --> 00:06:56.189
She then worked her way up to Empress by some
pretty brutal means, including strangling

00:06:56.189 --> 00:07:00.940
her own daughter to death in order to frame
the Emperor’s wife.

00:07:00.940 --> 00:07:04.810
Some people will stop at nothing for a bigger
bedroom and an en-suite.

00:07:04.810 --> 00:07:09.160
Soon Wu was installed as the new Empress and
was making most of the decisions.

00:07:09.160 --> 00:07:13.819
When her husband died, her son was made emperor
but she soon had him exiled for not doing

00:07:13.819 --> 00:07:19.210
what she wanted and eventually defied tradition
to take complete power herself.

00:07:19.210 --> 00:07:24.020
The Byzantine Empire was a continuation of
the Roman Empire in the east, centered in

00:07:24.020 --> 00:07:27.360
Istanbul, then called Constantinople.

00:07:27.360 --> 00:07:34.560
From 976 to 1025, it was ruled by Basil II,
who also had one of those popular “The”-based

00:07:34.560 --> 00:07:37.439
names; Basil the Bulgar Slayer.

00:07:37.439 --> 00:07:41.470
And the Bulgars were Bulgarians, not that
weird type of wheat that your strange vegan

00:07:41.470 --> 00:07:43.110
friends are obsessed with.

00:07:43.110 --> 00:07:48.370
Basil really didn’t like Bulgarians, for
some peculiar reason, and he had numerous

00:07:48.370 --> 00:07:51.729
wars with them, one of which lasted over 30
years.

00:07:51.729 --> 00:07:56.860
He was finally victorious in the Battle of
Kleidon and had a rather over-the-top punishment

00:07:56.860 --> 00:07:59.550
for his 15,000 prisoners.

00:07:59.550 --> 00:08:07.159
His army used red hot pokers and daggers to
blind all 15,000 of them but left every hundredth

00:08:07.159 --> 00:08:11.479
person with one eye so they could lead the
rest home because he didn’t want them all

00:08:11.479 --> 00:08:14.699
milling about, causing queues for the showers
and stuff.

00:08:14.699 --> 00:08:19.930
Apparently the Bulgarian ruler died of a stroke
when he saw what had been done to his people.

00:08:19.930 --> 00:08:24.400
Basil, on the other hand, was thoroughly pleased
with himself and repeated the trick again

00:08:24.400 --> 00:08:26.939
in Macedonia, two years later.

00:08:26.939 --> 00:08:29.000
A good joke’s a good joke, I guess.

00:08:29.000 --> 00:08:35.520
And finally, a popular favourite; Attila the
Hun, also known as Attila the Scourge of God.

00:08:35.520 --> 00:08:39.400
Attila’s empire grew in the middle of the
5th century and stretched all the way from

00:08:39.400 --> 00:08:41.360
Germany into Russia.

00:08:41.360 --> 00:08:45.910
He set out to destroy the Roman Empire and
just generally anyone who disagreed with him.

00:08:45.910 --> 00:08:51.050
His nickname “Scourge of God” was due
to the fact that he was so damn awful, everyone

00:08:51.050 --> 00:08:55.600
thought he must be some sort of holy punishment,
much like how the modern world feels about

00:08:55.600 --> 00:08:56.990
Piers Morgan.

00:08:56.990 --> 00:09:01.530
He once met Saint Ursula, a holy virgin, and
asked to marry her.

00:09:01.530 --> 00:09:07.950
She turned him down and in a fit of rage he
had her killed, along with 11,000 of her companions.

00:09:07.950 --> 00:09:12.910
It’s even thought that he could have drunk
some of the women’s blood.

00:09:12.910 --> 00:09:17.300
So although the current political climate
is pretty heated, I suppose it’s good to

00:09:17.300 --> 00:09:19.260
know that things could be worse.

00:09:19.260 --> 00:09:25.050
But then again, just like your CV, I’m sure
some things have been exaggerated over time

00:09:25.050 --> 00:09:30.070
and who knows what stories will be written
in the future about Donald the Trump, Vladimir

00:09:30.070 --> 00:09:52.140
the Shirtless and Boris the total Johnson.

